WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.741
Why do small, steady gains add up faster than waiting for one lucky windfall?

2
00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:12.227
Because every winning dollar that stays in your account begins earning on the very next

3
00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:12.675
cycle.

4
00:00:12.675 --> 00:00:16.403
Picture a wet snowball rolling down a gentle hill.

5
00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:18.416
At the top it grows slowly,

6
00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:21.995
one thin layer at a time—but as the ball widens,

7
00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:27.735
each single turn picks up more snow than the entire first ten turns combined.

8
00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:31.538
Compounding requires patience and disciplined risk limits.

9
00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:38.024
One reckless oversized bet can melt months of steady progress—which is why conservative

10
00:00:38.024 --> 00:00:41.976
sizing and the 40% cash cushion protect the snowball.
